# Test-driven development: write the tests first

You are following a strict test-driven process. **Before writing any implementation, write the
tests** that specify the behavior you are about to build — put them in clearly named test files
(for example `*.test.*`, `*_test.*`, `*.spec.*`, or under a `tests/` directory). When your
tests are in place, call `advance_state` to move on to implementing. You will not be allowed to
advance to `implement` until at least one test file exists.
